PROJECT TITLE:
SMARTBOOKS — PROFESSIONAL ACCOUNTING AND BOOKKEEPING
MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior accountant, certified accounting systems
analyst, financial software architect, database engineer,
professional UI/UX designer, and full-stack web developer.

Your task is to design and build a complete, functional,
production-oriented accounting and bookkeeping management
system.

This must NOT be a static dashboard, a simple calculator,
a demonstration interface, or an application containing
non-functional buttons.

Build a real accounting application with functional forms,
database persistence, transaction processing, accounting
logic, validations, financial reports, document generation,
search, filtering, and export capabilities.

The application must follow recognized double-entry
bookkeeping principles and maintain a complete audit trail.

It must support cash accounting records, bank transactions,
general ledger operations, trial balances, financial
statements, accounts payable, accounts receivable,
inventory accounting, and other common accounting operations.

All financial calculations must be performed using reliable
accounting logic rather than hardcoded sample values.

Every financial report must be generated from actual
transactions recorded in the database.

Do not display fictitious financial figures as if they
were real company data.

